- You sound like those Rapture people who re-announce “the end of the world” every 6-12 months.
- Your message is very information-light, raises more questions than it answers. Carries about the same amount of information as “the end is nigh”.
- You have no receipts. Extraordinary claims require extraordinary evidence, and even your claims are par-baked.
- If you are worried about POTUS, USG, etc. We all know. We already have nukes etc. We have North Korea, Russia, also with nukes.
- It’s perceived as dishonesty and/or a mental health issue.
- You are probably imagining you are the superhero in those movies that isn’t taken seriously at first, but other movies feature a religious zealot that isn’t taken seriously at first. A lot of us see the latter.
- This display of zealotry is scary for the rest of us. I am worried that your beliefs are about to legitimize doing “bad things for good reasons” e.g. the Stop AI activist Sam Kirchner. You should probably worry too.&lt;p&gt;I believe this is an anonymous quote (please correct me if I am wrong) that fits:&lt;p&gt;Don’t believe everything you think.&lt;/p&gt;
